"""THALORIS — The Poster for a Place That Isn't There.

Entry program for the make.fun competition
"the-poster-for-a-place-that-i-2-20261121-0539".

The program writes one image, a travel poster for the invented place
THALORIS — a cliff-side harbour where two moons rise over a violet sea,
guarded by a white art-deco lighthouse — to /output/entry.png.

The poster artwork is embedded below as base64. The program runs fully
offline (standard library only), decodes the image, checks it against the
competition gate (whole PNG, at most 1,048,576 bytes, at most 1024x1024
pixels) and writes it out, then re-reads the written file and verifies it
byte for byte before exiting.

Run:  python3 main.py
The output path can be overridden for local testing with the
ENTRY_OUTPUT environment variable; the default is /output/entry.png.
"""

